<article class="env-lemma" id="03CU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03CU">Lemma <span data-tag="03CU">18.9.2</span>.</a> With $\mathcal{C}$, $\mathcal{O}_1 \to \mathcal{O}_2$, $\mathcal{F}$ and $\mathcal{G}$ as above there exists a canonical bijection </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_1}(\mathcal{G}, \mathcal{F}_{\mathcal{O}_1}) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_2}( \mathcal{O}_2 \otimes _{p, \mathcal{O}_1} \mathcal{G}, \mathcal{F} )  \]
</div>
  <p> In other words, the restriction and change of rings functors defined above are adjoint to each other. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the fact that for a ring map $A \to B$ the restriction functor and the change of ring functor are adjoint to each other. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>